    "title": "Albany man accused of driving drunk with kids in car - NewsBreak",
    "text": "ALBANY, N.Y. ( NEWS10 ) — An Albany man is facing felony charges after police said he was driving drunk with two children in the car. Jerome Smith, 43, was pulled over for a traffic violation Tuesday evening in the area of Clinton Avenue and Quail Street in the city of Albany. Police said they smelled alcohol and noticed impairment. Smith then failed a field sobriety test. Police said there was a 1-year old and a 12-year old in the car at the time. There was also an adult in the car, who had a restraining order against Smith. He had previously been convicted of violating a restraining order against the same person, according to police. Smith refused a breath sample and was charged with criminal contempt, aggravated driving while intoxicated with a child in the vehicle, driving while intoxicated, endangering the welfare of a child, and several traffic violations. He was taken to the Albany County Jail. Read the latest from NEWS10: NEWS10 is the Capital Region’s local news leader! For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NEWS10 ABC.",
